			"id": "agent-analysis-dialog-overlay-example-triad-pipeline",
			"interpretation": "Five sibling overlay families (actionsheetview, alertdialogview, customdialog, popup, textpickerdialogview) repeat one triad: a @Builder/struct UI entry that opens a system overlay from a button click, an entity Map translating UI labels into ArkUI values or code snippets, and a viewmodel pair where an @Observed Descriptor extends CommonDescriptor and overrides convert(attributes: OriginAttribute[]) while a CodeGenerator implements CommonCodeGenerator.generate, returning a self-contained ArkTS sample string. Observable contract: overlay options (autoCancel, asymmetric transitions, sheetInfo, placement, canLoop, itemHeight, dialog style) come only from descriptor fields; convert switch-maps recognized names ('type', 'placement', 'dialogAlignment') and unknown names or unmapped values fall back via '?? this.x' and DEFAULT_KEY map entries. ActionSheetBuilder resolves UIContext from AppStorage (StorageKey.UI_CONTEXT) for showActionSheet; TextPickerDialogBuilder uses getUIContext().showTextPickerDialog with Toast accept/cancel callbacks; CustomDialogComponent owns two CustomDialogControllers (TipsDialog, CustomContentDialog from @kit.ArkUI), permits PRESS_BACK/TOUCH_OUTSIDE dismissal in onWillDismiss, picks a controller by descriptor.style, and nulls both controllers in aboutToDisappear. Public boundary: exported builders/structs, @Observed descriptor classes, CommonCodeGenerator implementations, and exported Map constants; cross-boundary bases CommonDescriptor/DescriptorWrapper plus @ohos/common (Toast, Logger, StorageKey). Maintenance duty: keep descriptor fields, mapping keys, and emitted snippets synchronized per family.",
